{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391354-men-in-malfeas","id":1391354,"title":"men in malfeas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-24T17:13:56-07:00","id":1391354,"title":"men in malfeas","content":"ok, so my last thread was a fail, I recognize my folly now. I am sorry to those I offended, and I hope to start fresh here. <br /> <br /> --------- <br /> <br /> my favorite parts of exalted are definitely the high fantasy aspects. Give me the supernatural realms over the directions any day of the week. I count the blessed isle as a not supernatural realm, no matter what its category is. one of my favorite realms is malfeas, the hell of the yozi's. I can't get enough of the yozi's and demons. but a fascinating concept that dosent get covered often is the human element. Namely what human cultures have arisen in hell. <br /> <br /> so I ask you, what human cultures live under the ever burning green sun. can be canon or homebrew, I don't care. but I do hope we don't get sidetracked by technicalities like my second titan war thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T17:48:49-07:00","id":1391363,"title":"","content":"I think the lore of 2e was that a regular human in Malfeas would die horribly from the <i>Nuclear Hate Radiation</i> given off by the green sun in a matter of minutes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T17:54:33-07:00","id":1391364,"title":"","content":"Well yes. But there was a rather interesting post on suffecent velocity called men in malfeas. So lets ignore the whole &quot;leger gives ultra cancer&quot; thing. Unless of course the civilization has an interesting way around it. Like oh, harvesting oramas's omen weather or using celcyean glass.<br /> <br /> Wrote this on my phone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T19:42:44-07:00","id":1391400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391354-men-in-malfeas?p=1391363#post1391363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the lore of 2e was that a regular human in Malfeas would die horribly from the <i>Nuclear Hate Radiation</i> given off by the green sun in a matter of minutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's quite a bit of an exaggeration. Liger's light is ever present, and described as maddening, but was not actually given any harmful characteristics, per se.<br /> <br /> However, the toxic air in Malfeas will kill a mortal in <i>exactly seven days</i> unless precautions are taken, such as an alchemical antidote or a living insect facemask (the Mayfly Mask). (CoCD : Malfeas, pg 19).<br /> <br /> There are, of course, other threats, and the weather is terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T19:44:18-07:00","id":1391401,"title":"","content":"Malfeas isn't just a place where demons live- it's their <i>prison, </i>so even if we ignore the Hate Radiation thing, we are left with this mandatory (and interesting!) question: <b>why are there humans in Demon-Jail?</b> It takes extremely powerful sorceries to get there, across a 5 day wide desert. <br /> <br /> Infernals are/were called the Green Sun <b>Princes</b>, and 2e lore was that they are treated <i>EXTREMELY</i> well in Malfeas. They inherit a lot of political power beyond the abilities of even many powerful demons. So maybe one of them has set something up? A Cult? A Seraglio? Palace staffed with humans to keep a sense of &quot;normalcy&quot;?<br /> <br /> TBH, the hammer and screwdriver in my Story Teller toolbox are &quot;A First Age Twilight Did It&quot; and &quot;The Magitek Thingamabob is slowly running out of juice&quot; so I wouldn't be surprised to find out that a First Age Twilight made a Malfeas Research Station like we have in Antarctica but then got herself kill in the Usurpation so now their descendants are stuck in a Science Dome completely cut off from the rest of the world for a thousand years, and that Science Dome is slowly breaking down, so they warped the Solars in with a Transdimensional Gate to fix it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T19:57:37-07:00","id":1391405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391354-men-in-malfeas?p=1391401#post1391401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malfeas isn't just a place where demons live- it's their <i>prison, </i>so even if we ignore the Hate Radiation thing, we are left with this mandatory (and interesting!) question: <b>why are there humans in Demon-Jail?</b> It takes extremely powerful sorceries to get there, across a 5 day wide desert.<br /> <br /> Infernals are/were called the Green Sun <b>Princes</b>, and 2e lore was that they are treated <i>EXTREMELY</i> well in Malfeas. They inherit a lot of political power beyond the abilities of even many powerful demons. So maybe one of them has set something up? A Cult? A Seraglio? Palace staffed with humans to keep a sense of &quot;normalcy&quot;?<br /> <br /> TBH, the hammer and screwdriver in my Story Teller toolbox are &quot;A First Age Twilight Did It&quot; and &quot;The Magitek Thingamabob is slowly running out of juice&quot; so I wouldn't be surprised to find out that a First Age Twilight made a Malfeas Research Station like we have in Antarctica but then got herself kill in the Usurpation so now their descendants are stuck in a Science Dome completely cut off from the rest of the world for a thousand years, and that Science Dome is slowly breaking down, so they warped the Solars in with a Transdimensional Gate to fix it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I work under two assumptions. Either some first age solar did it or they were humans who sided with the primordials and paid the price. but I want cool overworldly descendents. how has humanity adapted to a place where the sun never sets and silence means death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T21:06:36-07:00","id":1391414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391354-men-in-malfeas?p=1391401#post1391401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malfeas isn't just a place where demons live- it's their <i>prison, </i>so even if we ignore the Hate Radiation thing, we are left with this mandatory (and interesting!) question: <b>why are there humans in Demon-Jail?</b> It takes extremely powerful sorceries to get there, across a 5 day wide desert.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some mortals arrive hell through the wiles of infernal cults (as sacrifices, recruits, or both). Whether living or dead, mortal souls are valuable commodities, to be used as slaves, servants, cultists.<br /> <br /> And, apparently, some do manage to <i>just wander in</i> through the Endless Desert. <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It is easier to do so when you are not trying. Colonies of fugitives manage to eek out a grim existence amid the hellscape.</span></span></span></div><br /> Also there <i>are</i> &quot;backdoor&quot; routes out of Malfeas too; the Yozi cannot escape but under certain circumstances demons of each circle may enter Creation, and sometimes bring back soveniers.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malfeas, page 65</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On rare occasions, one of Cecelyne\u2019s sandstorms overtakes a ship of the Argosy while at the same time, a mortal\u2019s sand ship battles a sandstorm in Creation. If a mortal sailor dies a bloody death in the storm, the Argosy\u2019s ship passes from Hell to Creation, right by the other ship. The demonic sailors may attempt a little piracy of their own, taking the mortal sailors prisoner. The ship can return to Malfeas by sailing into the next sandstorm it finds, but the captain might decide to see what other fortunes Creation holds.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T21:23:40-07:00","id":1391421,"title":"","content":"That is true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T02:36:29-07:00","id":1391449,"title":"","content":"The best description and interpretation of Hell in Exalted is all from 1e, where it was weird an interesting and different, with psychedelic art depicting strange alien beings, and where the Yozis (weren't really called that back then) were more like places and natural hazards. Anyway! In that book Hell is pretty inimical to unprepared or unguided mortals on account of it 1) killing you within precisely seven days, and 2) lot of Blood Apes around etc. However. With proper preparation, one can survive the natural environment, and with a guide or patron or safe place to stay, one could easily spend extended periods of time there and do quite well. It's not like Neomah, for example, are naturally hostile or even unsympathetic to the plight of others. <br /> <br /> Even by accident, one could survive there. There's definitely scope for, as an example, a slave escaping into the desert, wandering into Malfeas accidentally, being found by an Agatae who develops a bizarre attachment to them (because they do that) and taking them to a convent of Neomah who then take them in, feed and clothe them as best they can, and take care of them. Perhaps they die after a week anyway, at which point the Neomah are confused and grieve, or perhaps they know of such things and bargain for an antidote to protect this mortal, who then lives with them. That is not particularly <i>likely</i> but it's entirely believable.<br /> <br /> As are many stories. Perhaps the slave encounters Ligier who has had a strange dream and wandered out to ponder it, encountered the slave, took a liking to them and blessed them with relief from the air of Malfeas, telling them that if they can survive by their wits and strength, the Demon City will bring them the freedom they never had.<br /> <br /> Like it's an alien world. It's often a very scary world. It's got some incredibly dangerous and hostile entities. But like, so is wandering the desert, lost and alone. So is getting shipwrecked. But it's survivable if you're lucky and come across the right locals/have a bit of will and grit to hang on. It's not Christian Hell. The things there aren't there just to torture you (although some will. You also might encounter an Agatae jealous of the colour of your eyes, which it then carefully gouges out, though it may then feel impossibly upset when you bleed out in front of it, and spend ages building a cairn above your body in memory) but rather they are... very alien.<br /> <br /> And if you are a Sorcerer who can find a way in, well, there's lots of possibility for power. It's not just a &quot;you're going to get betrayed and screwed,&quot; Demons can be pretty reasonable!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T06:45:49-07:00","id":1391471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391354-men-in-malfeas?p=1391449#post1391449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best description and interpretation of Hell in Exalted is all from 1e, where it was weird an interesting and different, with psychedelic art depicting strange alien beings, and where the Yozis (weren't really called that back then)</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about before Games of Divinity?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that book Hell is pretty inimical to unprepared or unguided mortals on account of it 1) killing you within precisely seven days,<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That was not in Games of Divinity.<br /> <br /> Another consideration for communities of humans in Malfeas might be descendants and associates of Demon-blooded humans. They accumulate these little communities that ultimately have to eke out some sort of living.<br /> <br /> I imagine that a lot of the time that's going to need finding a niche where you're in proximity to demons that can be bargained with or exploited to provide for your needs while also weak enough that they can't turn the tables on you. There are many Second Circle Demons who require some manner of spiritual resource from people, and it might be possible to strike up a system of patronage with them to provide something with greater convenience than they get in Creation in exchange for benefits.<br /> <br /> Mind, I'd say that mortal communities in Malfeas are uniformly young, and the typical fate is to be wiped out immediately by sudden disaster. Growth potential to offset extreme losses seems sharply limited; never mind the neighbours, where exactly is your food and water coming from? Barring mutations or blessings, I can only imagine a small amount of Hell's fare being edible to humans, and not in large enough quantity to facilitate a growing population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T07:06:00-07:00","id":1391475,"title":"","content":"IMO the best explanation for human populations in malfeas is that of slaves kept for prayers. The yozis know they need prayers to retain their power - and humans are... if nothing else... made for that purpose.<br /> <br /> so I can easily imagine that as part of their imprisonment, several loyalist communities, cults and perhaps even entire nations were exiled into malfeas. At this point they all probably bear the mutations of having interbred with the demons for quite a while, though their stock is likely continually replenished via people lured in from creation... or poor souls who don't get a choice in the matter<br /> <br /> it would make for a great plot element: Your players are trying to root out a demon cult, but they can't quite figure out what the cultists are doing - because they've been buying up salves by the hundreds, but there's no sign of human sacrifice. No blood, no remains, nothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...then they find the one-way portal room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T07:09:22-07:00","id":1391476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391354-men-in-malfeas?p=1391475#post1391475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The yozis know they need prayers to retain their power</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you basing that on?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T07:12:58-07:00","id":1391477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391354-men-in-malfeas?p=1391476#post1391476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are you basing that on?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That Authochon needs it. Says so in the MOEP: Alchies<br /> <br /> So it stands to reason that the yozis also gain nice things like essence and perhaps even extra willpower from worship?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T10:07:12-07:00","id":1391504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391354-men-in-malfeas?p=1391477#post1391477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That Authochon needs it. Says so in the MOEP: Alchies</div> </div> </div> </div>Autochthon is 1) Sick, and 2) Entirely cut off from the rest of existence. Neither of those is true of the Yozis.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo use an analogy, just because an asthmatic deep-sea diver needs an oxygen tank, doesn't mean his healthy-but-scarred brother in prison needs one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T10:10:07-07:00","id":1391505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391354-men-in-malfeas?p=1391504#post1391504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Autochthon is 1) Sick, and 2) Entirely cut off from the rest of existence. Neither of those is true of the Yozis.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo use an analogy, just because an asthmatic deep-sea diver needs an oxygen tank, doesn't mean his healthy-but-scarred brother in prison needs one.</div> </div> </div> </div>exaltly. Malfeas does not need humans. He hates humans. But he is also a being on par with Autocthon. Meaning he isn't likely to notice some civilizations in the endless layers of himself. and that's what I was asking for. not where the humans came from (unless its a part of there story) but how they adapted to survive in hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T10:42:56-07:00","id":1391509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391354-men-in-malfeas?p=1391477#post1391477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That Authochon needs it. Says so in the MOEP: Alchies<br /> <br /> So it stands to reason that the yozis also gain nice things like essence and perhaps even extra willpower from worship?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because he lives in elsewhere and is cut off from any form of external essence, That doesnt apply to any other primordial or yozi whatsoever.<br /> <br /> <br /> Answering the question. There can be a lot of reasons about why mortals or even mortal communities can be found in malfeas.<br /> <br /> Worshippers.<br /> Were sold as part of some deals.<br /> Were brough on by demons and thus are the property of one demon or another.<br /> Used as slave labor.<br /> Used for entertainment or prayers (not needing it doesnt mean its not pleasurable to be worshipped)<br /> <br /> Part of some intricated plan of a yozi.<br /> <br /> All of them would make their owners/ demons benefitting from them to protect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12829-tzimiscelord","name":"Tzimiscelord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T10:45:11-07:00","id":1391511,"title":"","content":"I think the devs said that the mortal death miasma is getting yeeted in 3e so yeah, a mortal presence there is more viable now than before.<br /> <br /> The low hanging fruit is to mirror the heaven's dragons and say there's a community of mortals and dragon blooded who have been living there for years. Maybe they were part of a cult that fled Creation, idk. Probably a load of demon blooded there too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T11:04:26-07:00","id":1391514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391354-men-in-malfeas?p=1391505#post1391505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> how they adapted to survive in hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna say that there have been times when the Exalted built themselves some kind of domicile in Malfeas adapted for their comfort, and even when long abandoned is capable of providing food, fresh water and good air for human needs.<br /> <br /> If a community wound up in Hell, such a place would have great value as shelter without needing to make much in the way of compromises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T13:02:44-07:00","id":1391531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1391354-men-in-malfeas?p=1391511#post1391511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> 